     "title": "Auspicious Dates for Marriage in January 2027",
     "content": "<img src=\"https://gcpimages.theweddingcompany.com/weddings/blogs/auspicious-hindu-wedding-dates-for-january/uploads/ec64dfd0-3be2-49a5-9465-5d42da428511.png\" alt=\"Photo of a  calendar showcasing Auspicious Dates for Marriage in January 2027\" title=\"Auspicious Dates for Marriage in January 2027\"><p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;\">Choosing the right wedding date is more than selecting a convenient day, it is a tradition deeply rooted in Hindu culture. The Shubh Muhurat, determined using the Panchang (Hindu Calendar), is believed to align marriages with positive energies, bringing harmony, prosperity, good fortune, and long-lasting happiness to the couple’s life.&nbsp;</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;\">For those planning to get married in January 2027, here are the auspicious marriage dates along with detailed Panchang information to help you choose the most favourable muhurat for your wedding.</span></p><p></p><div class=\"table-wrapper\"><table><tr><td colspan=\"1\" rowspan=\"1\" colwidth=\"165\"><p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;\">Date</span></p></td><td colspan=\"1\" rowspan=\"1\" colwidth=\"113\"><p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;\">Day</span></p></td><td colspan=\"1\" rowspan=\"1\" colwidth=\"192\"><p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;\">Shubh Muhurat</span></p></td><td colspan=\"1\" rowspan=\"1\" colwidth=\"166\"><p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;\">Nakshatra</span></p></td><td colspan=\"1\" rowspan=\"1\" colwidth=\"114\"><p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;\">Tithi</span></p></td></tr><tr><td colspan=\"1\" rowspan=\"1\" colwidth=\"165\"><h3><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;\">January 15, 2027</span></h3></td><td colspan=\"1\" rowspan=\"1\" colwidth=\"113\"><p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;\">Friday</span></p></td><td colspan=\"1\" rowspan=\"1\" colwidth=\"192\"><p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;\">7:15 AM - 2:13 PM</span></p></td><td colspan=\"1\" rowspan=\"1\" colwidth=\"166\"><p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;\">Revati</span></p></td><td colspan=\"1\" rowspan=\"1\" colwidth=\"114\"><p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;\">Saptami</span></p></td></tr><tr><td colspan=\"1\" rowspan=\"1\" colwidth=\"165\"><h3><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;\">January 18, 2027</span></h3></td><td colspan=\"1\" rowspan=\"1\" colwidth=\"113\"><p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;\">Monday</span></p></td><td colspan=\"1\" rowspan=\"1\" colwidth=\"192\"><p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;\">9:05 PM - 9:12 PM</span></p></td><td colspan=\"1\" rowspan=\"1\" colwidth=\"166\"><p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;\">Rohini, Kritika</span></p></td><td colspan=\"1\" rowspan=\"1\" colwidth=\"114\"><p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;\">Ekadashi</span></p></td></tr><tr><td colspan=\"1\" rowspan=\"1\" colwidth=\"165\"><h3><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;\">January 19, 2027</span></h3></td><td colspan=\"1\" rowspan=\"1\" colwidth=\"113\"><p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;\">Tuesday</span></p></td><td colspan=\"1\" rowspan=\"1\" colwidth=\"192\"><p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;\">7:49 AM - 7:15 AM (Jan 20)</span></p></td><td colspan=\"1\" rowspan=\"1\" colwidth=\"166\"><p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;\">Rohini, Mrigashira</span></p></td><td colspan=\"1\" rowspan=\"1\" colwidth=\"114\"><p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;\">Dwadashi / Trayodashi</span></p></td></tr><tr><td colspan=\"1\" rowspan=\"1\" colwidth=\"165\"><h3><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;\">January 20, 2027</span></h3></td><td colspan=\"1\" rowspan=\"1\" colwidth=\"113\"><p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;\">Wednesday</span></p></td><td colspan=\"1\" rowspan=\"1\" colwidth=\"192\"><p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;\">7:15 AM - 4:17 PM</span></p></td><td colspan=\"1\" rowspan=\"1\" colwidth=\"166\"><p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;\">Mrigashira</span></p></td><td colspan=\"1\" rowspan=\"1\" colwidth=\"114\"><p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;\">Trayodashi</span></p></td></tr><tr><td colspan=\"1\" rowspan=\"1\" colwidth=\"165\"><h3><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;\">January 24, 2027</span></h3></td><td colspan=\"1\" rowspan=\"1\" colwidth=\"113\"><p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;\">Sunday</span></p></td><td colspan=\"1\" rowspan=\"1\" colwidth=\"192\"><p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;\">10:20 AM - 9:29 PM</span></p></td><td colspan=\"1\" rowspan=\"1\" colwidth=\"166\"><p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;\">Magha</span></p></td><td colspan=\"1\" rowspan=\"1\" colwidth=\"114\"><p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;\">Tritiya</span></p></td></tr><tr><td colspan=\"1\" rowspan=\"1\" colwidth=\"165\"><h3><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;\">January 26, 2027</span></h3></td><td colspan=\"1\" rowspan=\"1\" colwidth=\"113\"><p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;\">Tuesday</span></p></td><td colspan=\"1\" rowspan=\"1\" colwidth=\"192\"><p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;\">8:18 PM - 7:14 AM (Jan 27)</span></p></td><td colspan=\"1\" rowspan=\"1\" colwidth=\"166\"><p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;\">Uttara Phalguni</span></p></td><td colspan=\"1\" rowspan=\"1\" colwidth=\"114\"><p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;\">Panchami / Shashthi</span></p></td></tr><tr><td colspan=\"1\" rowspan=\"1\" colwidth=\"165\"><h3><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;\">January 27, 2027</span></h3></td><td colspan=\"1\" rowspan=\"1\" colwidth=\"113\"><p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;\">Wednesday</span></p></td><td colspan=\"1\" rowspan=\"1\" colwidth=\"192\"><p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;\">7:14 AM - 11:56 PM</span></p></td><td colspan=\"1\" rowspan=\"1\" colwidth=\"166\"><p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;\">Hasta</span></p></td><td colspan=\"1\" rowspan=\"1\" colwidth=\"114\"><p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;\">Shashthi</span></p></td></tr><tr><td colspan=\"1\" rowspan=\"1\" colwidth=\"165\"><h3><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;\">January 30, 2027</span></h3></td><td colspan=\"1\" rowspan=\"1\" colwidth=\"113\"><p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;\">Saturday</span></p></td><td colspan=\"1\" rowspan=\"1\" colwidth=\"192\"><p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;\">3:55 AM - 7:13 AM (Jan 31)</span></p></td><td colspan=\"1\" rowspan=\"1\" colwidth=\"166\"><p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;\">Anuradha</span></p></td><td colspan=\"1\" rowspan=\"1\" colwidth=\"114\"><p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;\">Navami</span></p></td></tr><tr><td colspan=\"1\" rowspan=\"1\" colwidth=\"165\"><h3><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;\">January 31, 2027</span></h3></td><td colspan=\"1\" rowspan=\"1\" colwidth=\"113\"><p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;\">Sunday</span></p></td><td colspan=\"1\" rowspan=\"1\" colwidth=\"192\"><p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;\">7:13 AM - 7:34 PM</span></p></td><td colspan=\"1\" rowspan=\"1\" colwidth=\"166\"><p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;\">Anuradha</span></p></td><td colspan=\"1\" rowspan=\"1\" colwidth=\"114\"><p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;\">Dashami</span></p></td></tr></table></div><p></p><p></p><h2><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;\">15th January 2027, Friday</span></h2><h3><strong>Panchang</strong></h3><p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;\">Tithi: Saptami&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;\">Paksha: Shukla Paksha</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;\">Muhurat Timing: 7:15 AM - 2:13 PM</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;\">Vara: Shukravaar</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;\">Marking the return of the wedding season after Makar Sankranti, this auspicious Friday is blessed by Revati Nakshatra’s gentle grace and the prosperity of Shukla Paksha, creating a beautiful foundation for a harmonious and fulfilling married life.&nbsp;</span></p><p></p><a data-type=\"cta-banner\" class=\"twc-cta-banner\" data-cta-id=\"9396357a-7125-4364-b38e-0cd10cf8e2d5\" data-action=\"leadform\" data-align=\"center\" data-banner-name=\"Top Banner CTA\" style=\"--banner-w: 50.3%;\"><img src=\"https://gcpimages.theweddingcompany.com/weddings/blogs/auspicious-hindu-wedding-dates-for-january/uploads/12e86245-d2f1-49d9-8401-8dbf87304e12.webp\" alt=\"Top Banner CTA\" width=\"1600\" height=\"600\"></a><p></p><h2><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;\">18th January 2027, Monday</span></h2><h3><strong>Panchang</strong></h3><p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;\">Tithi: Ekadashi&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;\">Paksha: Shukla Paksha</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;\">Muhurat Timing: 9:05 PM - 9:12 PM</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;\">Vara: Somvaar</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;\">Guided by the steadfast energy of Rohini Nakshatra, this Shukla Dashami muhurat encourages emotional security, abundance, and a marriage rooted in warmth and mutual care.</span></p><p></p><p></p><h2><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;\">19th January 2027, Tuesday</span></h2><h3><strong>Panchang</strong></h3><p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;\">Tithi: Dwadashi / Trayodashi&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;\">Paksha: Shukla Paksha</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;\">Muhurat Timing: 7:49 AM - 7:15 AM (Jan 20)</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;\">Vara: Mangalvaar</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;\">Blessed by the curious and adaptable energy of Mrigashira Nakshatra, this Shukla Ekadashi muhurat encourages couples to build a marriage rooted in trust and strengthened through shared aspirations.</span></p><p></p><p></p><h2><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;\">20th January 2027, Wednesday</span></h2><h3><strong>Panchang</strong></h3><p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;\">Tithi: Trayodashi&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;\">Paksha: Shukla Paksha</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;\">Muhurat Timing: 7:15 AM - 4:17 PM</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;\">Vara: Budhvaar</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;\">A harmonious blend of Mrigashira’s graceful nature and Ardra’s transformative spirit, this Dwadashi muhurat symbolizes resilience, renewal, and enduring companionship.&nbsp;</span></p><p></p><p></p><h2><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;\">24th January 2027, Sunday</span></h2><h3><strong>Panchang</strong></h3><p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;\">Tithi: Tritiya&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;\">Paksha: Krishna Paksha</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;\">Muhurat Timing: 10:20 AM - 9:29 PM</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;\">Vara: Ravivaar</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;\">Punarvasu Nakshatra brings hope, renewal, and divine grace to this auspicious Shukla Purnima, making it a beautiful occasion to begin a marriage filled with happiness and lasting prosperity.&nbsp;</span></p><p><br></p><h2><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;\">26th January 2027, Tuesday</span></h2><h3><strong>Panchang</strong></h3><p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;\">Tithi: Panchami / Shashthi&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;\">Paksha: Krishna Paksha</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;\">Muhurat Timing: 8:18 PM - 7:14 AM (Jan 27)</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;\">Vara: Mangalvaar</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;\">The nurturing influence of Pushya Nakshatra lends this Krishna Dwitiya muhurat a sense of stability, prosperity, and unwavering support, qualities that form a foundation of a strong marriage.</span></p><p><br></p><a data-type=\"cta-banner\" class=\"twc-cta-banner\" data-cta-id=\"cebefc86-8fa8-4954-901f-dc19c7220e93\" data-action=\"leadform\" data-align=\"center\" data-banner-name=\"Bottom CTA\" style=\"--banner-w: 50.3%;\"><img src=\"https://gcpimages.theweddingcompany.com/weddings/blogs/auspicious-hindu-wedding-dates-for-january/uploads/c0f417e5-7a79-421c-b9e3-e754de84da8f.jpg\" alt=\"Bottom CTA\" width=\"1600\" height=\"600\"></a><p></p><h2><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;\">27th January 2027, Wednesday</span></h2><h3><strong>Panchang</strong></h3><p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;\">Tithi: Shashthi&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;\">Paksha: Krishna Paksha</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;\">Muhurat Timing: 7:14 AM - 11:56 PM</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;\">Vara: Budhvaar</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;\">With Pushya continuing to illuminate the day, the Tritiya muhurat is ideal for couples seeking a union blessed with harmony, wisdom, and enduring family happiness.</span></p><p><br></p><h2><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;\">30th January 2027, Saturday</span></h2><h3><strong>Panchang</strong></h3><p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;\">Tithi: Navami&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;\">Paksha: Krishna Paksha</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;\">Muhurat Timing: 3:55 AM - 7:13 AM (Jan 31)</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;\">Vara: Shanivaar</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;\">Uttara Phalguni Nakshatra brings its timeless symbolism of loyalty and enduring partnership to this Krishna Shashthi muhurat, making it especially meaningful for couples beginning a lifelong journey together.&nbsp;</span></p><p><br></p><h2><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;\">31st January 2027, Sunday</span></h2><h3><strong>Panchang</strong></h3><p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;\">Tithi: Dashami&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;\">Paksha: Krishna Paksha</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;\">Muhurat Timing: 7:13 AM - 7:34 PM</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;\">Vara: Ravivaar</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;\">With Uttara Phalguni giving way to Hasta Nakshatra, this Krishna Saptami muhurat beautifully blends steadfast devotion with creativity and harmony, offering an auspicious setting for vows that stand the test of time.</span></p><p></p><p>Read also: <a target=\"_blank\" href=\"https://www.theweddingcompany.com/wedding/auspicious-hindu-wedding-dates-in-april\">Auspicious Dates for Marriage in April 2026</a></p>",
